## Purpose
- Pin down the auth API contract and token/cookie behavior.

## Source of truth
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/Controllers/Auth/`
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/Controllers/Me/`
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/Configuration/JwtOptions.cs`
- `services/team-hub-auth/.env.example` (optional local `dotnet run`)
- `.env.staging.example` (Compose staging)
- `frontend/team-hub-web/src/app/core/auth/auth.service.ts`

## Do
- Use base route `/api/auth/v1` (API version `1.0`).
- Keep these endpoints:
  - `POST /api/auth/v1/register` -> `201 Created`, `400 Bad Request` on format validation errors (`ValidationProblemDetails`, `type=…/validation-failed`), `409 Conflict` on business validation errors (duplicate username/email) with `errors` payload (`type=…/conflict`).
  - `POST /api/auth/v1/login` -> `200 OK` with access token + user; request accepts `rememberMe` (boolean) to control persistent refresh cookie; errors as RFC 9457 `application/problem+json` (`invalid-credentials` / `account-locked` with `code`, `remainingAttempts`, `lockoutSeconds` extensions); `503 Service Unavailable` when Redis session store is down.
  - `POST /api/auth/v1/refresh` -> `200 OK` with rotated refresh token cookie, `401 Unauthorized` ProblemDetails if invalid/missing; `503 Service Unavailable` when Redis session store is down.
  - `POST /api/auth/v1/logout` -> `204 No Content` and cookie cleanup.
  - `POST /api/auth/v1/change-password` -> `204 No Content` after username + name + surname verification; revokes all refresh sessions and clears refresh cookies; `400 Bad Request` on format validation errors; `401 Unauthorized` ProblemDetails when identity verification fails.
  - `GET /api/auth/v1/me` -> `200 OK` current user (`id`, `username`, `email`, `name`, `surname`, `avatarUrl`); JWT required; `401` when missing/invalid.
  - `PATCH /api/auth/v1/me` -> `200 OK`; body `{ name?, surname?, email? }` (at least one field); username is not editable; `400` format; `409 conflict` on duplicate email (`errors.email`); JWT required; when email changes, revokes all refresh sessions and clears refresh cookies (re-login required for updated JWT email claim).
  - `POST /api/auth/v1/me/change-password` -> `204 No Content`; body `{ currentPassword, newPassword }`; JWT required; `401` when current password is wrong; revokes all refresh sessions and clears refresh cookies.
  - `PUT /api/auth/v1/me/avatar` -> `200 OK`; multipart `file` (JPEG/PNG/WebP, max 2 MB); JWT required; `400` validation; `503` when blob storage is not configured.
  - `DELETE /api/auth/v1/me/avatar` -> `200 OK`; JWT required; `503` when blob storage is not configured.
  - `GET /api/auth/v1/users` -> `200 OK` search results (`id`, `username`, `name`, `surname`; `email` empty); requires `q` min length 2 (else `[]`); matches name/surname/username; requires JWT Bearer; `401 Unauthorized` when missing/invalid.
- Access JWT includes `sub`, username, and `email` claims (`email` + `ClaimTypes.Email`) so organization `GET /me/invitations` can match pending invites.
- Keep register validation:
  - format (`400`): `name`, `surname`, `username`, `password` field rules.
  - business (`409`): duplicate `username` in `errors.username` (case-insensitive).
- Keep refresh token in `refreshToken` HttpOnly cookie (`SameSite=Lax`); when `rememberMe=false`, keep it session-scoped.
- Store refresh sessions in Redis (`auth:session:{refreshTokenHash}`) with TTL matching refresh token expiry; maintain `auth:user-sessions:{userId}` SET index for revoke-all. After rotation, the previous refresh token remains valid for 15 seconds.
- Keep `withCredentials: true` for login/refresh/logout in frontend clients.
- Restore the session on app start with one `/refresh` call; retry API `401` once after refresh.
- Keep refresh-token rotation with a short reuse grace window so concurrent `/refresh` calls do not drop the session.
- Keep JWT options from env/config: `Jwt__Key`, `Jwt__Issuer`, `Jwt__Audience`, `Jwt:ExpireMinutes`.
- Keep Redis connection from infrastructure: `Redis__ConnectionString` (Aspire injects; staging Compose sets `cache-redis:6379`).
- Keep PostgreSQL connection: Aspire `auth_db`; staging Compose `Host=db-postgres;...;Database=authdb;...` from root `.env.staging`.
- Keep blob storage from infrastructure Azurite / Azure (`BlobStorage__*` / Aspire `blobs`); user avatars live at `users/{userId}/avatar.{ext}`. Response `avatarUrl` is a read-only SAS URL.
- Keep auth health endpoint: `GET /health` checks PostgreSQL and Redis (`200` healthy, `503` unhealthy).

## Don't
- Do not return refresh token in response body.
- Do not loosen cookie security flags without explicit requirement.
- Do not introduce undocumented auth endpoints.

## Checklist
- Endpoint names and status codes match controller code/tests.
- Cookie name remains exactly `refreshToken`.
- JWT options are present before app start (`ValidateOnStart`).
